WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.500
Against the

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.935
backdrop of the Kremlin's

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.536
military struggles in Ukraine.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.070
Unpleasant.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.904
Vladimir Putin

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.239
says Russia will place

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.742
tactical nuclear weapons in Belarus.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.243
Ukraine's northern neighbor

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:10.977
or risk border

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.479
as both Ukraine and non-NATO

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.780
ally, Poland.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.081
It hasn't had a nuclear arsenal

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.516
since the end of the Cold War,

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.051
but that could change in

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.152
just a few months.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.253
Here's how Putin defended

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:24.190
the move
in an interview with Russian media.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.892
What you're seeing in this study,

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.360
the United States has done it

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.661
for decades.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.329
They have placed

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.930
their tactical nuclear weapons

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.399
in their ally countries,

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:33.833
NATO countries,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.202
in six countries, to be exact.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.938
Germany, the Netherlands, Belgium,

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.841
Italy, Turkey and Greece.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.643
And we had an agreement

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.112
with Lukashenko as allies do the same.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.313
Then you've been monitoring

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.982
reaction there in Ukraine

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:49.749
What have you been seeing

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.253
Well, what we see is that

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:53.953
the Ukrainians

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.155
clearly feel

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.524
that the temperature is being raised

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.426
by President Putin's statement

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.127
regarding the deployment

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.263
of tactical nuclear weapons

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:06.266
sometime down the line in Belarus.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.100
On the other hand,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.869
they are not pressing the panic button.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.137
We did see a statement

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.238
from Aleksey

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.039
Daniel of who's

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.674
a senior adviser to President

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.142
Vladimir Zelensky.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.609
He said,

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.644
and I'm reading here

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.611
Putin's statement

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.880
about placing nuclear weapons in Belarus

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:24.017
a step towards internal destabilization

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:24.918
of the country.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.885
Maximizes

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:26.986
the level of negative

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.222
perception and public rejection

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.023
of Russia.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.559
And Putin in Belarus, Russian society.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.460
The Kremlin,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.595
he concluded, took Belarus

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.597
as a nuclear hostage.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:40.700
I think if you read between the lines

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.436
here,
what do the Ukrainians are saying

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.539
that Lukashenko, whose hold on power

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.541
just a few years ago was looking

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.709
rather shaky

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.645
may be weakening his domestic position

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.949
by allowing Russia at some point

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:59.285
to deploy nuclear weapons in Belarus

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.587
and as.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.223
As Matthew just mentioned,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.557
the fact that this means

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.892
more Russian troops

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.894
in Belarus, a country

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.762
which did allow the Russians

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.464
to use their territory

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:14.601
to invade Ukraine just over a year ago.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.202
All right.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.738
And then, Ben, from the battlefront now.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.472
What's the latest

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.007
particularly in the ongoing battle

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.342
for Bakhmut

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.512
Well, the situation there

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.580
continues to be precarious.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.282
CNN was on the phone

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.451
with a senior official spokesman

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.254
for Ukrainian forces in eastern Ukraine.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:37.123
He said that the Russians in the area

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.024
around Bakhmut

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.759
do not seem to be suffering

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.060
from a shortage

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.462
of artillery shells,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.664
that the shelling of that city

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.032
continues to be intense.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:46.799
He says that

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.500
there are around

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.537
4000 civilians incredibly

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:54.841
still inside what's left of that city.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.442
Now, every day

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.644
we're seeing that the Russians

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:58.444
have advanced

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.279
in some areas,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.480
the Ukrainians

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.482
claiming that they're pushing back

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:03.483
and others.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.551
What's most important

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.752
is that
there is one

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:09.255
last road allowing for Ukrainian forces

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.724
to go in and out of the city

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.494
and to bring supplies and whatnot.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.962
That road continues

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.330
to be quite dangerous.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.465
And if if at some point

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.834
the Russians do manage to either

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.002
cut that road

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.371
or make it impassable because of fire,

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:26.573
that could spell

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:27.440
the end

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.509
of the Ukrainian military presence in

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.443
Barmore can.

